    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDetached private residence set on generous and mature grounds with a west and south facing rear aspect. Situated in a highly popular and excellent location on the Maree Road in Oranmore, less than a 5 minute walk to the main street in the village.\n\nOriginally constructed circa 1992, Shanlin House has the rare combination of a convenient village location for a generous property on a large, private plot. Beautifully cared for and upgraded over the years, the property is presented to the market with quality finishes, a spacious layout and an aspect that maximises natural light in the main living spaces which overlook the private grounds. Perfectly suitable to modern needs, there is a choice of living accommodation, a home office, a beautiful open plan kitchen area while each bedroom is complete with an ensuite. An adjoining 'granny flat' is an excellent feature to this home and offers a range of options. Externally, the landscaped gardens include lawns with flower and shrub beds along with a perfectly positioned rear patio area, all enclosed by mature, private boundaries. A storage shed and garden studio are also located to the rear.\n\nShanlin House is a wonderful property overall featuring space, quality and privacy in an excellent location. Oranmore is a thriving coastal village and one of the most sought-after locations in the wider region. There are excellent services and major employment hubs in the area in addition to schools, shops and many popular restaurants. It is also close to Galway Bay Golf Club and Galway Sailing Club while Galway City is a short 10 km drive away."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nVia tiled porch, solid timber hallway, coved ceiling, storage.\n\nReception Room: - \nSolid oak floor, coved ceiling, front aspect window, French doors to dining room.\n\nFamily Room: - \nSolid oak floor, coved ceiling, front aspect window, gas fire with beautiful brick fireplace.\n\nStudy: - \nPerfect home office, built in desk & storage, timber floor, rear aspect window.\n\nKitchen: - \nLarge open plan kitchen with living area to rear. Tiled floor, solid timber kitchen with granite worktop, integrated dishwasher, fridge freezer, double oven, & electric hob.\n\nLiving Area: - \nBright, dual aspect space with bay window, tiled floor, feature red brick chimney breast with stove, direct access to private, west facing rear garden.\n\nDining Room: - \nSolid timber floor, bay window, coved ceiling.\n\nUtility Room: - \nTiled floor, built in storage with sink & plumbed for washing machine, rear aspect window & side door.\n\nGuest WC: - \nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin, side aspect window.\n\nBedrooms 1-7: - \nTimber floor, front/side/rear aspect window, built in/fitted wardrobe.\n\nEn-Suites 1-7: - \nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin, shower.\n\nBathroom: - \nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin, bath, separate shower, side aspect window.\n\nGranny Flat: - \nOne bedroom unit with kitchen, living, bathroom, bedroom & utility room.\n\nAttic level: - \n3 storage rooms, shower room.\n\nGarden: - \nExternally, the landscaped gardens include lawns with flower and shrub beds to the front and rear. The boundary hedging is mature and provides excellent privacy for the perfectly positioned rear patio area. A storage shed and garden studio are also located to the rear.\n\n"
      },
